#%PAM-1.0
# cosmic-greeter's lock screen: the service name is fixed in its binary
# (src/locker.rs). It runs as the user, authenticates and checks the account.
# The login screen is another service, cosmic-greeter-login (greetd's
# `service` in /etc/greetd/cosmic-greeter.toml), so that a finger can unlock
# the screen but never logs in.
#
# Fingerprint (the fingerprint system extension, see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-24-fingerprint-design.md): the lock screen
# shows PAM's messages, so the finger comes first ("Place your finger on the
# reader"), and the password prompt follows after 10 s or three tries, at
# once for a user with no finger enrolled or a machine with no reader.
# pam_fprintd.so comes only with the extension, and a line that starts with
# "-" is skipped when its module is missing: without the extension the stack
# is the login one, as before.
-auth      sufficient   pam_fprintd.so  timeout=10
auth       include      login
-auth      optional     pam_gnome_keyring.so

account    include      login
